.TH YTM-DL 1 "2026" "ytm-dl 0.4.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ytm-dl \- minimal TUI for bulk-downloading YouTube Music albums, EPs and singles
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ytm-dl
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIFILE\fR | \fILINK\fR[,\fILINK\fR...]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
A small wrapper around
.BR yt-dlp (1)
that downloads many YouTube Music links in parallel and shows their status in a
minimal monochrome terminal UI.
With no argument it asks for input. The input may be a path to a text file, several
links separated by commas, or a single link.
.PP
In a text file, links may be separated by commas, new lines, or both.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-out " \fIDIR\fR"
Output directory. Default: ~/Music/ytm-dl.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-format " \fIFMT\fR"
One of mp3, m4a, opus, flac. Default mp3. Giving this option skips the format picker.
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-jobs " \fIN\fR"
Number of links downloaded in parallel. Default 2.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-cookies " \fIBROWSER\fR"
Use cookies from a browser (for example firefox) to reduce throttling and bot checks.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Pass \-v to yt-dlp and keep the logs of failed links in OUT/.logs.
.TP
.B \-\-plain
No TUI: process one link at a time and show yt-dlp's own output. This is also used
automatically when stdin or stdout is not a terminal.
.TP
.B \-\-example
Print an example links file.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a short usage text.
.SH KEYS
In the format picker: up/down to move, 1-4 to jump, Enter to confirm, q to quit.
While downloading: q cancels. When finished, any key exits.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B YTM_DL_DIR
Output directory (same as \-\-out).
.TP
.B YTM_DL_FORMAT
Default format; when set, the format picker is skipped.
.TP
.B YTM_DL_JOBS
Parallel links. Default 2.
.TP
.B YTM_DL_STALL
Seconds without any new bytes before a link is killed and retried. Default 60.
.TP
.B YTM_DL_RETRIES
Automatic retries per link. Finished tracks are skipped on retry. Default 2.
.TP
.B YTM_DL_COOKIES
Browser to take cookies from (same as \-\-cookies).
.TP
.B YTM_DL_VERBOSE
Set to 1 for verbose yt-dlp output and kept logs.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I OUT/<album>/<NN - title>.<ext>
Downloaded tracks. A single-track link is saved in its album's folder, or in
.I OUT/Singles/
when it has no album.
.TP
.I OUT/.archive
yt-dlp download archive. Tracks listed here are skipped on later runs.
Delete it to download everything again.
.TP
.I OUT/.logs/
Logs of failed links.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
ytm-dl
ytm-dl links.txt
ytm-dl -f flac -j 3 links.txt
ytm-dl 'https://music.youtube.com/playlist?list=OLAK5uy_...'
ytm-dl --plain -v links.txt
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 if every link succeeded, 1 if any failed, 130 if cancelled.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR yt-dlp (1),
.BR ffmpeg (1)
